=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_9c3a — The late cook: kitchen goes quiet until 18:30 (fork of p_789a)

Fork of p_789a. The parent's cooking window (pan on counter 17:30–19:00) is contradicted by the 18:00 patrol: the pan is still in the cupboard_k1 at 18:00, and only appears on the counter_k1 at 19:00. The pot follows the same pattern — cupboard at 18:00, counter at 18:00 (one sighting) but the 19:00 pass confirms it on the counter. The knife is in the drawer at 18:00 and on the counter at 19:00.

This means the actual cooking start is closer to 18:30, not 17:30. Between 17:30 and 18:30 the kitchen is still in its pre-cooking state: pans in the cupboard, knives in the drawer, the cutting board on the counter (it lives there). The residents are probably still finishing work, washing up, or setting the table.

I shifted the cooking blocks from 17.5–19 to 18.5–20 for pan, pot, and knife. The cutting board stays on the counter all day (it is its resting spot). The rest of the evening ritual (TV, remote, blanket, snack bowl) is unchanged from the parent.

What would refute this fork: pan_shared sighted on counter_k1 at 18:00 on a weekday; or the remote still at tv_stand_l1 at 20:00.

